  "historical_output_text": " Here are instructions for planting a seed:\n\n1. Choose a spot in your garden where the seed will get enough sunlight. Most seeds require at least 6 hours of direct sunlight daily to grow. If you're planting flowers, choose a spot with slightly more sun. If you're planting vegetables, you'll want a spot with direct sun for most of the day. \n\n2. Prepare the soil. Loosen the top few inches of soil with a garden fork or trowel. Remove any weeds or debris. Adding some compost or well-rotted manure can help the soil retain moisture and provide nutrients for the seed.\n\n3. Plant the seed at the recommended depth. Check the seed packet for depth guidelines, which vary by species. Generally, seeds should be planted about 2-3 times as deep as they are wide. Planting too shallowly can make them dry out, while planting too deeply can hinder their ability to sprout.\n\n4. Cover the seed with soil and gently pat down. This helps seal in moisture and provides support as the seed germinates. Don't pack the soil too tightly, which can prevent the roots from growing.\n\n5",
